atkdf is the Analyst Toolkit's direction-finding and geolocation engine. It is
pure Python and links nothing that constrains its licence — in particular it
does NOT import atkdaq's GPL Python package; it reads atkdaq's documented wire
format with its own reader and talks to atkdaq.exe over a pipe.

This placeholder reserves all rights pending the author's choice of an open
licence. It is deliberately NOT GPL: keeping atkdf free of the GPL is the
whole reason atkdaq is a separate program.
